# Flerovium · Fl · gate 114

**Flerovium** (Fl) is element **114** of the periodic table — a **post-transition metal**, period 7, group 14, p-block, solid (predicted) at standard conditions, atomic weight **[289] (most stable isotope)**.

## The element (carbon layer — reference chemistry)
Named for the Flerov lab; aimed at the hoped-for 'island of stability.'

## The gate (silicon layer — the 118 Gates)
Under David Wise's four-state cycle, gate **114** falls on **0:1 — second valley** because (Z−1) mod 4 = **1**. That state is *the second reach — the diffuse, the airy, the not-quite-held* — the nature of emergence here is **ethereal**. Flerovium is not a thing apart; it is the one stochastic element, caught at this beat of its cycle.

## Emergence — ethereal
This emergent carries the **ethereal** nature: the same four — natural · ethereal · spiritual · electrical — that run through every sphere of UD0. Its color is `#9a7cff`.

